  "attestation_verification_boundary": {
    "capture_time": "Each successful run's in-run TAR was verified twice with gh attestation verify: once with GitHub CLI's default trust configuration and once with the downloaded bundle plus a captured trusted root. Both used exact repository, workflow, signer digest, source digest, source ref, predicate, and hosted-runner constraints.",
    "post_run_finalization": "Completed-state GitHub API recapture and the three-row final join occur after the workflow completes. They are checksum-bound and identity-validated but are not part of the GitHub-builder-attested in-run TAR.",
    "repository_verify_mode": "The --verify command re-performs cryptographic verification for every successful in-run TAR against its captured trusted root and then enforces exact certificate, Rekor timestamp, statement, subject, builder, source, ref, runner, and invocation fields.",
    "semantic_limit": "The attestation authenticates the archive digest and builder identity; it does not establish the semantic truth of workflow-controlled predicate or event data.",
    "trust_bootstrap": "Offline re-verification is reproducible relative to the captured root bytes. The captured root is not self-authenticating; the capture-time default-trust verification and an optional fresh online check provide the external trust bootstrap."
  },
  "claim_boundary": "Nine preserved, separately identified first-attempt workflow outcomes form a balanced three-version by three-repeat controlled cohort. Successful runs hold one protocol commit, workflow, kind binary, workload, subject digest, and hosted-runner class constant while changing the pinned Kubernetes minor version. The repeats show procedural repeatability only; no confidence interval, failure-rate inference, or production reliability claim is made. A capture-time public API observation records that each exact tag had one workflow invocation; that observation is checksum-bound but not a signed API response. The GitHub attestation authenticates the in-run TAR only. Completed-state recapture and finalization are checksum-bound and identity-validated, not builder-attested. The workflow generates the joining identifier. This is not identifier discovery, cross-provider or cross-organization replication, a field deployment, or external reproduction.",
  "kind_version": "v0.32.0",
